# Reactor Geometry

## 1. Project Objective

This project investigates the computational modelling of multiphase systems involving non-Newtonian fluids using ANSYS Fluent.

The primary objective is to develop a CFD model of a 2D fluidized-bed reactor to investigate multiphase flow behaviour, phase distribution, and liquid-phase collection using an internal Y-shaped collector.

The study aims to understand the interaction between gas, liquid, and solid phases and evaluate the influence of the internal collector geometry on liquid-phase collection and reactor performance.

---

## 2. Reactor Configuration

The computational domain consists of a **2D vertical fluidized-bed reactor**.

### General Configuration

- **Model:** 2D planar
- **Reactor orientation:** Vertical
- **Coordinate system:** X-Y plane
- **X-axis:** Horizontal direction
- **Y-axis:** Vertical/upward direction
- **Axisymmetric:** No
- **Sector model:** No
- **Periodic boundaries:** No

The reactor contains an internal **Y-shaped structure** designed specifically for **liquid-phase collection**.

The Y-shaped structure is intended to:

- Collect the liquid phase from the reactor
- Provide a pathway for liquid collection
- Facilitate subsequent liquid recirculation
- Allow investigation of the effect of internal geometry on liquid-phase behaviour

The Y-shaped structure is **not intended to collect the gas or solid phases**.

The collected liquid will subsequently be recirculated using a pump. The pump itself will not be explicitly represented as a physical pump geometry in the 2D computational domain.

